00:35:27.890 --> 00:35:31.480
We're then using our Cloud
storage load component

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:35.050
to connect into a flat
file, which is stored

00:35:35.050 --> 00:35:37.270
in a Cloud Storage bucket.

00:35:37.270 --> 00:35:39.400
And it will copy the
contents of that flat file

00:35:39.400 --> 00:35:42.780
down into BigQuery.

00:35:42.780 --> 00:35:45.070
In parallel, we're checking
for an if condition,

00:35:45.070 --> 00:35:48.210
so we're checking if some data
already exists within BigQuery.

00:35:48.210 --> 00:35:51.030
And then we're loading some
data up from Google Analytics.

00:35:54.010 --> 00:35:57.550
We're also loading out some
data from Microsoft SQL Server

00:35:57.550 --> 00:36:01.100
from our on-premise system.

